      ],
      "content": "HIGH STREET 1. 5252                                                   (East Side)                                                   No 41 (The King's Arms                                                   Public House) TL 0507 1/17              18.6.48. II*                       GV 2. Early C17.  Timber frame, plaster faced road front, deep modillioned eaves beneath steeply tiled roof.  3 storeys, 5 windows.  Modern ground floor bay windows 1st floor early C19 3 light sash window.  Back wing half timbered with 1st floor open gallery Known as The King's Arms since the early C17.  VCH, II, p 215. Nos 41 to 47 (odd) form a group. Listing NGR: TL0558507823"
    }
